claim.claim-text:
5. A broad band, multi-band radar detector comprising a receiving antenna, a microprocessor controller, a first mixer, a swept frequency first local oscillator, a second mixer, a second local oscillator, a third mixer, a third local oscillator, signal processing circuits for processing signals input thereto from said third mixer, and output means for outputting visual and/or audio output signals in response to output signals from said signal processing means which indicate the reception by said receiving antenna of incoming radar signals in any frequency band of interest; wherein said first mixer has a signal input port into which signals from said receiving antenna are applied, a local oscillator input port into which signals from said first local oscillator are applied, and an output port from which signals at a first intermediate frequency are derived; wherein said first local oscillator is under the control of said microprocessor, whereby said first intermediate frequency signal is derived at one of a first high intermediate frequency/, and a second low intermediate frequency/; wherein said second mixer has a signal input port into which signals at either of said first high intermediate frequency/, and said second low intermediate 

frequency / are applied, a local oscillator input port into which signals from said second local oscillator are applied, and an output port from which signals at a second intermediate frequency are derived; wherein a first pair of parallel signal paths and a first single pole, double throw switch means having a first switch position and a second switch position, are interposed between said first mixer and said second mixer; wherein the first of said first pair of parallel signal paths has a bandpass characteristic at a selected one or the other of said frequencies/ and/ so that a first intermediate frequency signal from said first mixer at said selected frequency will be fed to the input port of said second mixer when said first switch is in said first switch position, and the second of said first pair of parallel signal paths has a bandstop characteristic at the same selected frequency whereby a signal at the other of said first intermediate frequency signal frequencies/, and/ will be fed to the input port of said second mixer when said first switch is in said second switch position; wherein said second intermediate frequency is fed to a signal input port of said third mixer, signals at a preselected frequency are fed from said third local oscillator to a local oscillator port of said third mixer, and signals at a third intermediate frequency are derived from an output port of said third mixer for further signal handling; wherein a second single pole, double throw switch having a first switch position and a second switch position is interposed between said second mixer and said third mixer, and a second pair of parallel signal paths is interposed between said first switch and said second switch; wherein the first of said second pair of parallel signal paths is arranged so as to provide a straight signal path between said first switch and said second switch when said second switch is in its first switch position, so as to bypass said second mixer; and wherein the second of said second pair of parallel signal paths is arranged between said first switch and said second mixer, so as to provide a signal path through said second mixer when said second switch is in its second switch position; 

 whereby, when said first switch is in either of its first or second switch positions and said second switch is in its second switch position, said radar detector functions as a triple conversion radar detector, having down conversion at each of said first, second, and third mixers; and whereby, when said first switch is its second switch position and said second switch is in its first switch position, said radar detector functions as a dual conversion radar detector, having down conversion at each of said first and third mixers.
